; Strict-warning regression for the generated code: this (inline_tests)
; library compiles its modules with -w +a -warn-error +a, the harshest
; user regime, so every warning the PPX-generated code provokes is a
; build failure here. The fixture exercises let%test, module%test, and
; let%expect_test with every payload family (tagged, quoted, exact, bare,
; output), so every shape the desugaring emits — the registration call,
; the expect calls over the sanitized output, the constrained config
; reference — compiles clean. The tests themselves pass; the regression
; is the build.

(library
 (name windtrap_test_ppx_strict)
 (inline_tests)
 (flags
  (:standard -w +a -warn-error +a))
 (preprocess
  (pps ppx_windtrap)))
